The vertices are $(i+0.5, j+0.5)$, $(i+0.5, j-0.5)$, $(i-0.5, j+0.5)$, $(i-0.5, j-0.5)$.
The squared distances are:
$d_1^2 = (i+0.5)^2 + (j+0.5)^2$
$d_2^2 = (i+0.5)^2 + (j-0.5)^2$
$d_3^2 = (i-0.5)^2 + (j+0.5)^2$
$d_4^2 = (i-0.5)^2 + (j-0.5)^2$

We need $\max(d_1^2, d_2^2, d_3^2, d_4^2) \le R^2$.
